<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dar es Salaam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dar es Salaam is the largest city and chief port of Tanzania, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> coast. Founded in the 1860s by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Majid of Zanzibar, it became the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-east-africa">German East Africa</a> in 1891 and the starting point of the Central Railway to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-tanganyika">Lake Tanganyika</a>. It remained the capital under British rule and after independence, although <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dodoma">Dodoma</a> has since been designated the official capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dar-es-salaam.jpg" alt="Dar es Salaam" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Stanley from Nanaimo, Canada · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Joseph%27s_Catholic_Cathedral_(34895613805).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
